# `sink`'s mailbox depth is 1, and the first `send` fills it, so a good
# name sent to `sink` raises `mailbox full`. `ghost` is no Script of the
# Group, so a good name sent to it raises `object gone`. Every bad name
# raises its own error first, and no `send` record follows it: 42 and a
# list are `wrong kind` with `expected` `"text"`, even to the receiver 7;
# `all`, the Reserved Word `send`, text with a space, empty text, a
# Selector with too few arguments, one part, an excluded label (`in`) or
# no closing colon are `bad message name`. `with` is a contextual word, not
# a Reserved Word, so it names a message and reaches `object gone`. A
# waiting send and a Join Member check the name the same way.
